---
import '../styles/home.css';

const siteUrl = 'https://foxwarm.550w.host';
const githubUrl = 'https://github.com/550W-HOST/foxwarm';
const installCommand = `curl -fsSL ${siteUrl}/install-foxwarm.sh | bash`;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Foxwarm is a self-hosted workspace for persistent AI agents, long-running sessions, tools, and optional Nodes and Channels." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f36a2f" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Foxwarm — persistent AI agents in your own workspace" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Run persistent AI agents with tools, memory, optional execution Nodes, and the channels you choose." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={siteUrl} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={siteUrl + '/'} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32x32.png" sizes="32x32" />
    <title>Foxwarm — persistent AI agents in your own workspace</title>
    <script is:inline>
      (() => {
        const saved = localStorage.getItem('foxwarm-site-theme');
        const preferred = matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = saved || preferred;
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Foxwarm home">
        <img class="fox-mark" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="28" height="28" />
        <span>Foxwarm</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href={`${githubUrl}#readme`}>GitHub</a>
        <button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme" title="Switch color theme">
          <span class="theme-icon" aria-hidden="true">◐</span>
        </button>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Self-hosted agent workspace</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Keep the thread.<br />Own the workspace.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Foxwarm gives AI agents persistent sessions, practical tools, and memory that lives with your own installation—not inside a disposable chat tab.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/docs/installing/">Install Foxwarm</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/">Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="install-line" aria-label="Linux, macOS, and WSL install command">
            <code>{installCommand}</code>
            <button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy={installCommand} aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <p class="requirements">Requires Git, Node.js 20+, npm, and tmux. Windows has a native PowerShell installer.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="system-map" role="img" aria-label="Illustration: users reach Foxwarm through WebUI or Channels; Sessions connect models and persistent memory to tools running locally or on optional Nodes.">
          <p class="visual-label">Illustrative system map</p>
          <div class="map-top">
            <div class="map-chip"><span aria-hidden="true">◉</span> WebUI</div>
            <div class="map-chip"><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span> Channels</div>
          </div>
          <div class="map-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="map-core">
            <div class="core-head"><img class="mini-fox" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="22" height="22" /><strong>Foxwarm</strong><small>your instance</small></div>
            <div class="session-card">
              <span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div><strong>project/main</strong><small>persistent session</small></div>
              <span class="running">running</span>
            </div>
            <div class="context-row"><span>Memory</span><span>History</span><span>Skills</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="map-branches" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="map-bottom">
            <div class="map-node"><span>◇</span><strong>Models</strong><small>provider you choose</small></div>
            <div class="map-node"><span>⌁</span><strong>Tools</strong><small>files, shell, MCP</small></div>
            <div class="map-node"><span>⬡</span><strong>Nodes</strong><small>optional execution hosts</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Built for work that continues</p>
          <h2 id="principles-title">More than a prompt box</h2>
          <p>A compact runtime that connects the parts of an agent workflow without pretending they are the same thing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="feature-index">01</span>
            <h3>Persistent by design</h3>
            <p>Sessions survive restarts. Long conversations are compacted into traceable layers, with archive-backed recall when earlier context matters.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="feature-index">02</span>
            <h3>Agents have a home</h3>
            <p>An Agent owns a long-lived workspace and memory. Give it several Sessions for separate threads without splitting its identity.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="feature-index">03</span>
            <h3>Tools where work happens</h3>
            <p>Use built-in file and shell tools, reusable Skills, MCP servers, and optional Nodes for another machine or environment.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="feature-index">04</span>
            <h3>Your model, your channels</h3>
            <p>Connect supported OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic model providers. Start in WebUI, then add messaging Channels only when you need them.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="path" aria-labelledby="path-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> From zero to first session</p>
          <h2 id="path-title">A short path to a useful local agent</h2>
        </div>
        <ol>
          <li><span>1</span><div><strong>Install</strong><p>Run the installer on Linux, macOS, WSL, or Windows. Program files and runtime data stay separate.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>2</span><div><strong>Choose a model</strong><p>Open the tokenized local WebUI and finish first-run setup with your provider, model ID, and API key if required.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>3</span><div><strong>Start working</strong><p>Use the default Agent and Session, attach a Skill, or create a focused thread. Add Nodes and Channels later.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="final-callout" aria-labelledby="final-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Ready when you are</p>
          <h2 id="final-title">Run Foxwarm on your machine.</h2>
          <p>Start with WebUI and one model. The rest is optional.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="final-actions">
          <a class="button light" href="/docs/installing/">Installation guide</a>
          <a class="text-link" href={githubUrl}>View source on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <a class="brand" href="/"><img class="fox-mark" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="26" height="26" /><span>Foxwarm</span></a>
      <p>Self-hosted, open source, and MIT licensed.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href="/docs/">Docs</a><a href={githubUrl}>GitHub</a><a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>License</a></nav>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      document.querySelector('.theme-toggle')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const next = document.documentElement.dataset.theme === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = next;
        localStorage.setItem('foxwarm-site-theme', next);
      });
      document.querySelector('.copy-button')?.addEventListener('click', async (event) => {
        const button = event.currentTarget;
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy || '');
        const previous = button.textContent;
        button.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = previous; }, 1400);
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
